Runs the node-side Agent Access probes top-down and prints one line per
check (pass / warn / fail / skip): [mcp_relay] valid, enrolled with an
org that answers /healthz, the agent-access registration, ONE STS token
mint for the first approved vserver (the token is never printed or
stored), every journaled client config still routing its stdio entries
through the relay, the launch journal's backups and bindings, and the
hash-chained decision record. Exits non-zero when any check fails.

With [mcp_relay].enabled = false no network probe runs; it only checks
that no client config is left wrapped.

Usage:
  observer mcp doctor [flags]

Flags:
      --config string   path to config.toml (default ~/.observer/config.toml)
  -h, --help            help for doctor
      --json            print JSON
